window.AKK_FARMING_IMMORTALITY_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_FARMING_IMMORTALITY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: Testing Spiritual Roots","paragraphs":["\"Hurry! All children under ten years old in the village, gather at the village entrance right now!\"","A rushed shout carried all the way from the eastern end of the village, startling the sparrows in the trees into fluttering wildly into the air.","\"The immortal sect is here to recruit disciples!\"","The previously quiet Great Tree Village instantly erupted into chaos.","\"An immortal sect? Is that for real?\"","\"Of course it's real! The immortal master is right at the village entrance, and we only have a quarter of an hour—no late admittance. Anyone with little kids should hurry and bring them over, who knows, they might have a predestined fate with cultivation!\"","\"This old man has lived for more than sixty years, and this is the first time I've ever heard of such a thing. Could this be a scam?\"","\"Can a scammer fly down from the sky?\"","Those words immediately silenced all the villagers who still harbored doubts. In just a few moments, the hundred-year-old old pagoda tree at the village entrance was packed full of people.","A dozen still-ignorant children were pushed to the front by their parents, all craning their necks, looking at the blue-robed woman under the tree with a mix of fear and curiosity.","The woman looked no more than twenty years old, her long hair held back only by a single jade hairpin, the hem of her spotless robe completely free of dust. Even though she was standing right in the middle of the crowd, she seemed separated from the surrounding dirt and noise by an invisible barrier.","A slightly bold little boy asked in a soft voice, \"Are you an immortal master?\"","The woman glanced down at him, her expression calm, not haughty in the slightest.","\"I am not an immortal, just a cultivator.\"","The moment her voice fell, she waved her hand, and everyone's vision blurred for a second before a half-human-tall gray-white stone platform appeared out of thin air under the old pagoda tree. A collective gasp rose from the crowd.","Chen Su paid no mind to the crowd's amazement, and simply said, \"Line up, place your hands on the stone platform one by one. We will find out immediately if you have spiritual roots.\"","The adults quickly herded their children into a long line.","The first child stepped forward trembling, placed a hand on the platform, and the stone did not react at all.","Chen Su glanced at them, and said calmly, \"No spiritual root. Next.\"","The second, the third, the fourth.","\"No spiritual root.\"","\"No spiritual root.\"","\"Still no spiritual root.\"","The same words repeated over and over.","The villagers, who had been full of hope at first, gradually fell quiet. Some of the children who had been tested were still confused, while others had already understood they had not been selected, and walked back to their parents with their heads hanging low.","Before long, the last child stepped back, and the stone platform had not lit up with even the tiniest glimmer of light the entire time. Chen Su was not surprised by this—among ordinary mortals, those with spiritual roots were one in ten thousand.","\"Fine then.\"","Chen Su raised her hand, just about to put away the spirit testing platform, when a rush of footsteps suddenly came from the distance.","\"Immortal Master! Wait, Immortal Master!\"","A tall, broad-shouldered man came running from the end of the village path, huffing and puffing, holding two little girls in his arms.","He had run so fast that his forehead was covered in sweat, and the front of his tunic was soaked through, but he did not even bother to catch his breath before speaking urgently, \"Immortal Master, my two daughters were playing by the river earlier, and I wasted time looking for them. Please give them one more chance!\"","Chen Su glanced up at the sky. The quarter of an hour had already passed.","But in the end, she did not refuse, and only said softly, \"Come forward.\"","\"Thank you Immortal Master, thank you so much Immortal Master!\"","Qin Ye thanked her repeatedly, quickly setting his elder daughter down. The two little girls looked nearly seven years old, sharing seven out of ten similar facial features. The older girl was quiet and composed, while the younger one stared at the spirit testing platform with wide round eyes, full of unmasked curiosity.","\"Zhenzhen, you go first.\"","Qin Ye held his elder daughter's hand and led her to the stone platform. Qin Zhen glanced up at Chen Su, then placed her palm on the platform as she was told.","A few moments passed, and the platform did not react at all.","Chen Su said, \"No spiritual root.\"","The light in Qin Ye's eyes dimmed for a second, but Qin Zhen simply pulled her hand back quietly, showing little disappointment, and instead turned to look back at her little sister.","\"Jiajia, it's your turn.\"","\"Okay.\"","Qin Jia leaned out from her father's arms, stretched out her small, fair little hand, and pressed it smack onto the stone platform.","\"It's cool.\"","The second her words ended, the stone platform shook violently. Chen Su's originally calm expression changed drastically, and in the next instant, a dazzling white light shot straight up into the sky from the platform! A biting cold spread out in all directions, and the noisy village entrance fell completely silent in the blink of an eye.","Chen Su stared intently at the spirit testing platform, her breath catching for a split second. Pure white spiritual light, cold aura seeping out, not a single trace of any other attribute mixed in.","\"A top-grade ice spiritual root!\"","Her usual steady voice carried a clear, obvious fluctuation for the very first time. To make sure she had not misread it, Chen Su poured another wisp of spiritual energy into the spirit testing platform.","It really was a top-grade ice spiritual root. Waves of shock surged through Chen Su's mind. The Qingyun Sect had not taken in a disciple with such exceptional talent in nearly a hundred years. As long as this child did not meet an untimely death halfway through her cultivation, she would at least reach the Nascent Soul realm in the future, and might even have a shot at touching the path of Soul Transformation.","She had come down the mountain only to complete a routine sect mission, never expecting to find such a once-in-a-generation unpolished jade in this remote little village.","\"Wonderful, wonderful, wonderful!\"","Chen Su said three \"wonderful\"s in a row, a rare hint of joy appearing in her eyes. She put away the spirit testing platform, squatted down, and did her best to make her voice sound gentle.","\"What is your name?\"","\"My name is Qin Jia.\"","The little girl blinked, then corrected earnestly, \"The Jia that means praise, not the jia that means home.\"","The corners of Chen Su's lips lifted into a faint smile.","\"Qin Jia, would you like to come with me to the Qingyun Sect to practice cultivation?\"","\"What is cultivation?\"","\"Once you cultivate, you can fly on a sword, cast magical spells, and even pull items out of thin air the way I did just now.\"","Qin Jia's eyes lit up instantly.","\"Is that like doing magic tricks?\"","Qin Ye, who was holding her, turned bright red with panic, terrified that his daughter's innocent, childish words had offended the cultivator, but he did not dare to interrupt rashly. Chen Su was not offended at all.","\"Something like that.\"","Qin Jia immediately clapped her hands excitedly. \"I want to learn! I want to learn how to whoosh things out of nowhere!\"","Seeing that more and more villagers were gathering around, and the murmurs of discussion were growing louder, Chen Su frowned slightly.","\"This is not a good place to talk. Take me to your home.\"","Qin Ye nodded hurriedly. \"This way, Immortal Master.\"","The Qin family's home was not far from the village entrance. Before the group had walked even a few steps, most of the villagers in the whole village had followed after them. After all, for such a remote mountain village, an immortal sect recruiting a disciple was a once-in-a-hundred-year event, especially since the one chosen was the Qin family’s younger daughter that everyone knew.","Once they stepped through the Qin family's courtyard gate, Chen Su lifted a finger and tapped gently, and an invisible barrier instantly wrapped around the entire house. The chattering voices of the villagers outside cut off abruptly, leaving Qin Ye both shocked and awed.","Just a moment ago, it had been as noisy as a market outside, but now not even a sliver of sound could get through. Such a feat was completely beyond the comprehension of ordinary mortals.","Before long, all the members of the Qin family had gathered in the main hall. The Qin family did not have a complicated household structure.","The grandfather Qin Huai, grandmother Wang Sumei, the eldest son Qin Ye and his wife Liu Zhen, and the second son Qin Wen. The two little girls Qin Zhen and Qin Jia were each held tight in one of Qin Ye's hands.","Chen Su got straight to the point. \"I am a disciple of the Qingyun Sect. Qin Jia possesses a top-grade ice spiritual root, with exceptional cultivation talent. If she joins our sect, she will be able to walk the great path of eternal life in the future.\"","The Qin family did not fully understand exactly what a top-tier ice spirit root entailed, but they could tell from Chen Su's earlier reaction that such a natural gift was extraordinarily rare.","Qin Ye remained silent for a long time before he spoke hesitantly. \"Immortal Master, Jiajia is only six years old. Could we wait a few more years until she is a bit older before she leaves with you?\"","Liu Zhen's eyes immediately turned red the moment she heard this. Qin Jia was still so young that she would occasionally wake up crying for her mother in the middle of the night. How could she bear to let her daughter go off all alone to a completely strange place?","\"Cultivation must begin at a young age. The Qingyun Sect only accepts children under ten years old, and the younger the child, the easier it is for them to draw qi into their bodies. If this window of opportunity is missed, their path to immortality could be cut off entirely.\"","The room fell completely quiet in an instant.","\"Then maybe she just won't go.\"","Qin Ye spoke out of the blue, leaving everyone stunned, even Chen Su who lifted her eyes slightly in surprise.","Qin Ye held his little daughter tighter in his arms, his voice growing tight with emotion. \"I'm just an unlearned hunter. I don't know anything about the great path of cultivation, nor do I understand the pursuit of immortality and long life. All I know is that she is still too young. She can't bear to leave her parents, and we can't bear to be separated from her either.\"","Liu Zhen could no longer hold back her tears and turned her head to wipe them away. Qin Jia did not understand why the adults had all gone quiet all of a sudden, so she simply reached out and wiped the sweat off her father's forehead.","\"Don't be sad, Daddy.\"","Qin Ye's eyes grew warm with tears.","Chen Su was silent for a moment before speaking slowly. \"If Qin Jia only had an ordinary spirit root, I would not say another word. But a top-tier ice spirit root is extremely rare. If she stays in the mortal world, she will turn to nothing but a handful of loess a hundred years from now. But if she embarks on the path of cultivation, she could live for hundreds of years, or even far longer than that.\"","\"On top of that, she will not be left all alone in the cultivation world. The sect will arrange for her housing, food, clothing, and personal instruction, and she will take a master as her teacher.\"","Qin Huai hesitated for a moment before he could not help but ask, \"Immortal Master, can we go with her together? Jiajia is really too young. Even if only her mother is allowed to stay by her side to take care of her, that would be enough.\"","Chen Su frowned. In the cultivation world, most ordinary families who learned their child possessed such a rare gift would be overjoyed beyond words, rushing to send their child to the immortal sect as soon as possible. This was the first time she had ever come across a family that, faced with such a tremendous opportunity, only cared about their child being too young. But then she thought to herself that the mortal world was after all different from the cultivation world, and her tone softened a little.","\"Mortals are not permitted to enter the cultivation world where the Qingyun Sect resides. The spiritual energy there is so dense that those without spirit roots cannot withstand it with their physical bodies, and anyone who ventures in rashly will end up with their meridians shattering completely.\"","The faces of all the Qin family members turned pale at once.","Chen Su continued, \"However, just outside the cultivation world, there is a city called Neighboring Immortal City that is connected to Qingyun Sect's teleportation array. You can settle down near Neighboring Immortal City. After Qin Jia enters the sect, she can use the sect's teleportation array to travel and meet you once every year.\"","A flicker of emotion crossed Qin Ye's face. Meeting once a year, though still a long stretch of time apart, was far better than never seeing each other for the rest of their lives.","\"Then she will go. Now that there is still a chance for us to meet again, I cannot stand in the way of my daughter's great opportunity,\" Qin Ye said, his throat tight with emotion.","\"I want to go!\"","Qin Jia, who had been standing quietly to the side, spoke up all of a sudden, drawing everyone's gaze to her.","She clearly did not truly understand what parting meant, and said excitedly, \"I want to learn magic tricks from Fairy Sister. Once I learn them all, I will come back and perform for Daddy, for Mommy, for Grandfather and Grandmother, and also for my elder sister!\"","As she spoke, she wriggled about in Qin Ye's arms, nearly slipping right out of his hold.","\"Jiajia, be still.\"","Qin Zhen spoke suddenly, and Qin Jia froze immediately, quickly covering her mouth with both hands, leaving only her big bright eyes darting around. She was fearless of everyone else in the family, but she was just a little afraid of this usually quiet elder sister of hers. Qin Zhen gently patted her father on the arm.","\"Daddy, put me down.\"","Qin Ye did as she said and set her on the ground. Qin Zhen did not look at Chen Su, but turned to her grandfather Qin Huai first.","\"Grandfather, let us all go to Neighboring Immortal City.\"","Qin Huai was slightly taken aback.","\"Our Qin family only moved to Big Tree Village a few years ago. We have no farmland here, no ancestral property at all. Daddy and my uncle are skilled hunters, Grandfather can make fine bows and arrows, and Mommy and Grandmother are good at sewing, mending, and cooking.\"","Though she was still young, she spoke in a clear, orderly manner.","\"If we could make a living in Big Tree Village, we can make a living in Neighboring Immortal City too. If we stay here, my little sister will have to leave all by herself. But if we move to Neighboring Immortal City, she can come see us every year, and our family will never truly be separated.\"","She paused for a moment, then turned to look at Qin Jia. The little girl still had her hand over her mouth, her eyes shining brightly as she looked back at her.","Qin Zhen said softly, \"My little sister has such a precious chance. We should not let her give it up just because we cannot bear to part with her.\"","Chen Su glanced at Qin Zhen. Earlier during the spirit root test, this girl had shown no resentment at all when she learned she had no spirit root of her own. Now that her younger sister had obtained such an extraordinary natural gift, she felt not a hint of jealousy, but had immediately come up with a perfect plan that satisfied everyone.","Such strength of character was even more precious than a spirit root, Chen Su thought to herself with a quiet sigh, it was truly a pity.","Qin Huai did not say a word for a long time after listening to his granddaughter's words, until at last he let out a heavy sigh.","\"Zhenzhen is right.\"","He looked over at his eldest son.","\"Ye'er, we will go with Jiajia.\"","Wang Sumei nodded through her tears. \"Yes, let's go. It's far better than being separated by thousands of miles, never getting to see each other for the rest of our lives.\"","Liu Zhen held Qin Ye's hand. Tears were still rolling down her cheeks, but her tone was firm.","\"We will all go together.\"","Qin Ye looked down at the little daughter in his arms, then over at his elder daughter standing beside him, his eyes filled with nothing but reluctance.","After a long while, he spoke in a hoarse voice. \"All right.\"","\"We will go to Neighboring Immortal City.\"","Qin Jia finally let go of her hand covering her mouth and cheered out loud.","\"Hooray! We're all going together!\"","The heavy, oppressive atmosphere in the main room finally lifted a little with her cheerful cry, and Chen Su quietly let out a breath of relief. Such a top-tier talent had not slipped through her fingers after all. At that moment, Chen Su had no idea that the fate that would be changed by this encounter with immortal opportunity that day would not be limited to Qin Jia alone.","Seeing that the Qin family had made their decision, Chen Su said no more. She swept her hand over her storage bag, and two pale green jade pendants appeared in her palm.","The pendants were shaped like crescent moons, identical in size and pattern. If the two were fitted together, they would form a perfect full moon.","\"This item is called the Concentric Pendants.\"","Chen Su handed one pendant to Qin Jia, then held the other out to Qin Zhen.","\"They were originally low-grade artifacts used by sect disciples to locate their traveling companions. I have made some modifications to them, and inscribed a mutual sensing formation inside.\"","Qin Zhen did not take it right away, but looked up at her and asked earnestly, \"Can they let us find my little sister?\"","\"They can only sense the general distance, not point out the exact location. The farther apart you are, the dimmer the light from the pendants will grow. The closer you are, the brighter the light will shine. Even if you are thousands of miles apart, the light will be almost invisible to the naked eye, but if you calm your mind and focus, you will still be able to see a faint glimmer.\"","Qin Ye could not help but ask, \"What if the light goes out completely?\"","Chen Su fell silent for a brief moment.","\"These pendants have already recognized each of the two girls as their respective masters.\"","\"As long as the other owner of the jade pendant is still alive, there will remain a wisp of light within the jade pendant. If one owner passes away, the light in the other jade pendant will be completely extinguished, and cracks will begin to form on the pendant's body right after.\"","The main hall fell completely silent in an instant, and Liu Zhen subconsciously hugged the little daughter in her arms tighter.","Qin Jia, however, did not grasp the gravity of the situation at all. She only held up her own half of the jade pendant high, and asked excitedly,","\"Then if I put mine together with my sister's, will it turn into a full moon?\"","Chen Su nodded.","\"When they are close enough, the two pendants will draw towards each other. If they are pressed together, they will briefly merge into one whole.\"","Qin Jia immediately leaned out from her father's embrace, and held her jade pendant out to her elder sister.","\"Sister, let's try it!\"","Only then did Qin Zhen take the other half that belonged to her. The moment the two crescent-shaped jade pendants drew near, they both lit up with a pale cyan glow. As the light blended together, the two pendants gently pulled against each other, fitting together seamlessly to form a full round moon, making Qin Jia's eyes sparkle with delight.","\"It really turned into a full moon!\"","Qin Zhen looked down at the round moon formed in her palm, her fingers tightening slightly around it. After a few moments, the two jade pendants separated on their own. Chen Su threaded thin cords through the small holes on each pendant, and fastened them around the two sisters' necks respectively.","\"Keep them close to your bodies, and do not take them off lightly.\"","\"The United Hearts Pendants can only sense distance and life and death. They cannot transmit voices, nor can they shield you from danger, but as long as the light in the pendant remains, you will know that the other person is still safe and sound.\""]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: Sisters Reunited","paragraphs":["A full year had slipped by in the blink of an eye.","Over the past twelve months, the Qin family had spent nearly every day on the road. Before Chen Su left, she had left the Qin family a sum of silver and a map leading to the City of Neighboring Immortals. The Qin party had trekked over mountains and crossed rivers, weathered days of nonstop heavy rain, and fended off bandits lying in wait along the paths. Against all odds, they had finally arrived safely.","The City of Neighboring Immortals was the mortal city closest to the cultivation realm, and on occasion, cultivators from immortal sects would come and go through its gates. Most of the residents within its walls were noble lords, aristocrats, and wealthy merchant clans, all drawn there chasing the sliver of a chance at immortal fate. If a family struck that lucky break, they could rise to prominence in a single leap. It was precisely for this reason that every inch of land in the City of Neighboring Immortals was worth its weight in gold.","The entire Qin family stood outside the city gates, watching the constant stream of ornate horse-drawn carriages coming and going through the entryway, and fell quiet for a moment. They had traveled for an entire year, trekking every step of the way, only to realize they could not even afford a foothold inside the city walls.","Qin Huai pondered for a long time, then lifted his gaze to the rolling, lush mountains stretching beyond the city. \"We can't afford to live in the city, so we won't live there,\" he said slowly, leaning on his wooden staff. \"Our Immortal Master only told us to settle down near the City of Neighboring Immortals, she never said we had to live inside its walls. As long as we are close enough that Jiajia can find us when she comes back, it does not matter where we make our home.\"","Qin Ye nodded in agreement. \"Father is right. We were hunters to begin with. We can make a good living relying on the mountains.\"","Qin Huai looked at his two sons. \"Ye, Wen, go into the mountains and find a place suitable for us to settle.\"","\"We know, Father,\" Qin Ye and Qin Wen said in unison.","The two brothers slung their bows over their shoulders, took their firewood knives, and quickly vanished into the forest. The rest of the Qin family stayed behind to rest at the foot of the mountain.","As dusk fell, Qin Ye hurried out of the woods, his tunic hem dotted with dry leaves, but a bright, excited grin on his face. \"Father, I found a spot!\"","Qin Huai stood up immediately. \"What's it like?\"","\"There's a cave halfway up the mountain. It's dry inside, and there's no sign any wild beasts have ever lived there. Little Wen stayed behind to clear the cave entrance, and sent me back to bring all of you there.\"","Wang Sumei nodded repeatedly as she listened. \"There's water nearby, and it keeps out the wind and rain. That's more than good enough.\"","But Qin Huai was still cautious. \"Are there any footprints of ferocious beasts nearby?\"","\"Wen and I checked the whole area. We didn't find any. There are only tracks left by hares and pheasants.\"","\"Then let's go take a look.\"","The whole group picked up their bags and followed Qin Ye up the mountain. After walking for more than half an hour, they finally spotted the cave. A wide, open flat stretch of land lay just outside its mouth.","\"Mother, sister-in-law, you two rest for a little while first.\"","The Qin family did not waste any time, and quickly set to work tidying the place up. Qin Zhen did not laze about either. She carried armfuls of dry firewood thicker than her own arms, running back and forth to help.","\"Starting tomorrow, Ye, Wen and I will build two wooden huts outside the cave,\" Qin Huai said.","Qin Ye added, \"Wen and I can go hunting in the mountains. The City of Neighboring Immortals has a big population, so game meat and furs should sell for a good price. We can save up silver little by little, and life will get better for sure.\"","Wang Sumei smiled warmly. \"When we first arrived at Dashu Village, the place we lived in was worse than this spot. As long as we're all together as a family, we'll never be unable to make ends meet.\"","At the words \"as a family\", Liu Zhen's hand holding a clay bowl paused slightly. A family, she thought, there is still one missing from us.","Qin Zhen slipped her hand inside her collar, gently closing it around the cool jade pendant she wore. \"Grandfather,\" she said.","\"Hmm?\" Qin Huai responded.","\"Will Jiajia know we're here?\"","Qin Huai looked at her and spoke in a soft, gentle voice. \"Our Immortal Master said that when the time is right, Jiajia will come back. She has a matching jade pendant too. As soon as she gets near the City of Neighboring Immortals, the two of you will know, through the pendants.\"","Qin Zhen nodded quietly. \"I understand.\" She did not ask any more questions, but her hand never loosened its grip on the jade pendant.","At that very moment, thousands of miles away in the Qingyun Sect, the night was deep. A peak covered in snow all year round jutted up above a sea of clouds.","By the side of the frozen lake at the top of the peak, a little girl in a bright red disciple robe sat cross-legged in meditation. Her fair, soft little face was flushed pink from the biting cold. Her eyes were closed, and her hands rested neatly on her knees. But after only a short while, her eyelashes fluttered furtively.","A little later, she sneaked one eye open and glanced over to the side. Chen Su was standing by the edge of the ice lake, looking down at a jade slip in her hand. She did not seem to have noticed the little girl's small, secret movement.","Qin Jia let out a quiet sigh of relief, and carefully shifted her leg, which had gone numb from sitting still for so long.","\"Sit properly,\" Chen Su said, without even lifting her head.","Qin Jia's leg, which had just barely lifted off the ground, dropped right back down. She puffed out her cheeks and mumbled under her breath, \"Senior Sister wasn't even looking. How did she know I moved?\"","\"Divine sense,\" Chen Su replied.","\"When will I get to learn divine sense?\"","\"When you reach the Foundation Establishment stage, you will naturally develop your divine sense.\"","Qin Jia's face immediately fell. Her lively, outgoing nature had not settled down at all even after she joined the immortal sect. Every day, she was either pestering her master, or trailing after Chen Su, asking one question after another.","At first, Perfected Person Binghua had thought her new little apprentice was cute and full of charm. But after just a few days, she got such a headache from the endless stream of questions that she passed Qin Jia over to Chen Su. Qin Jia was absolutely delighted by the arrangement, since she had always liked Chen Su a great deal.","Quiet fell over the ice lake again. Qin Jia closed her eyes, and tried her best to follow the cultivation method to sense the spiritual energy floating between heaven and earth.","All of a sudden, a faint warm tingle spread from her chest. The warmth was so faint that she would never have noticed it if she had not been sitting perfectly still.","Qin Jia reached for her collar on instinct, and grabbed the jade pendant tucked inside. \"Sister!\" she cried out.","Qin Jia jumped right up from the ground. The cold air that had gathered all around her scattered in an instant.","Chen Su frowned. \"Qin Jia.\"","\"Senior Sister, my sister is here!\" Qin Jia completely forgot about her cultivation lesson, and ran toward Chen Su holding the jade pendant. She was running so fast that she nearly tripped over the long hem of her robe, and stumbled forward.","\"Slow down,\" Chen Su said, reaching out to steady her.","Qin Jia did not even stop to catch her breath. She held the jade pendant high up in front of Chen Su, her voice cracking with excitement. \"Senior Sister, look! It's glowing!\"","Chen Su glanced down at the pendant. \"They have arrived,\" she said.","Qin Jia froze for a split second, then jumped for joy so hard her whole body bounced. \"Father's here! Mother's here! My sister must be here too!\" She threw her arms around Chen Su's arm and shook it hard. \"Senior Sister, I want to go to the City of Neighboring Immortals right now! This very second!\"","Chen Su glanced at the darkening sky. \"It's far too late now. The teleportation array is closed for the night.\"","The big grin on Qin Jia's face vanished at once. She looked up at Chen Su, her eyes full of disappointment. \"What about tomorrow?\" She pouted, her shoulders slumping.","Chen Su looked at her dejected little face. \"Tomorrow, when the teleportation array opens, I will take you there.\"","In the next instant, Qin Jia lit up all over again. \"Senior Sister is the best in the whole world!\" She threw herself at Chen Su and wrapped her arms around her waist, grinning so wide her teeth were on full display.","Chen Su looked at the little girl clinging to her, and sighed helplessly. \"Let go of me first.\"","\"No,\" Qin Jia mumbled, burying her face against Chen Su's sleeve.","\"Go back and continue your cultivation practice.\"","\"My sister and my whole family are here now, how could I possibly calm down enough to focus on cultivation?\"","Chen ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍Su was just about to respond, when a lazy voice drifted down from the top of the mountain peak. \"If you can't calm down, then you don't have to cultivate.\"","Perfected Person Binghua had appeared out of thin air above the ice lake. She wore a flowing white silk dress, standing barefoot in mid-air, her features cold and strikingly beautiful. In her hand, she held a string of bright red spirit fruits.","\"My disciple of Binghua won't get left behind by others just because she skips one night of practice,\" Perfected Person Binghua said.","Chen Su bowed and greeted her, \"Master.\"","Qin Jia immediately let go of Chen Su and spun around to run toward Perfected Person Binghua. \"Master!\"","Perfected Person Binghua swept her up into a hug, then pressed a string of spirit fruits into her hand. \"You've been missing your family, haven't you? Tomorrow, your senior sister will take you home. Bring whatever you want with you. I won't have people thinking that a disciple of mine has to go home empty-handed.\"","Qin Jia nodded so hard her braids bounced. \"I'll bring Grandfather a longevity-nourishing pill, Grandmother a soft bolt of cloth, Father and Uncle the archery gear from the immortal sect, and Mother a beautiful hairpin.\"","She paused, then counted on her fingers again earnestly. \"And I have to bring something for my elder sister too.\"","Perfected Person Binghua asked casually, \"What does your sister like?\"","Qin Jia tilted her head and thought for a long time. What did her sister like? Her gaze landed on the spirit fruits in Perfected Person Binghua's hand. \"My sister loves growing things. Back at home, she was always the one who helped Mother plant all the vegetables.\"","Perfected Person Binghua chuckled. \"Growing mundane vegetables is hardly any remarkable skill.\"","But Qin Jia said very seriously, \"The vegetables my sister grows taste better than anyone else's.\"","She took a bite of the spirit fruit in her hand. After a couple of chews, her little face crumpled up. \"Sour!\"","Perfected Person Binghua did not look the least bit concerned. \"This is a jade spirit fruit. It was never meant to be a snack for you.\"","\"Then I'll take the seeds back for my sister,\" Qin Jia declared right away. \"The ones she grows will definitely be sweeter than this one.\"","Perfected Person Binghua was amused by her. \"Spirit plants are nothing like mortal vegetables. Without spiritual energy to nourish them, the seeds might not even sprout.\"","Qin Jia did not care about that at all. She carefully tucked the half-eaten fruit pit into her storage pouch, then held out her hand to Perfected Person Binghua. \"Master, do you have more?\"","\"How many do you want?\"","\"Lots and lots.\"","Perfected Person Binghua flicked her sleeve, and over a dozen jade boxes of different shapes landed in front of Qin Jia. They were just some low-grade spirit plants and spirit rice seeds she had picked up over the years and never bothered to plant. \"Take all of them.\"","Qin Jia happily stored every last jade box away. She did not care how valuable the seeds were. In her mind, anything from the immortal sect had to be wonderful.","Down below, Qin Zhen suddenly ducked her head. The jade pendant on her chest was growing warm, and its light was getting brighter and brighter.","She understood immediately. \"Grandfather.\"","Qin Huai was outside the cave sorting out his bows and arrows, and he turned around at her call. Qin Zhen had already rushed out of the cave, the most uncharacteristically hurried she had been all year.","\"Jiajia is here.\"","Every member of the Qin family froze. The wooden bowl in Liu Zhen's hand clattered to the ground. \"What did you say?\"","Qin Zhen pulled the jade pendant out from under her collar. She looked up toward the direction of Immortal's Neighbor City, her eyes shining bright. \"The pendant is glowing. Jiajia is close by.\"","Liu Zhen's eyes welled up with tears at once. \"Let's go meet her!\"","The whole family quickly gathered their things and hurried down the mountain path. The closer they got to the foot of the mountain, the brighter the jade pendant in Qin Zhen's hand glowed. Then, through the clouds, a sword shot through the air. On the flying sword stood two figures, one tall and one small. Qin Jia spotted her family standing at the foot of the mountain from far away. She froze for a second, then leaned over the edge of the flying sword and waved as hard as she could.","\"Sister!\" Her clear voice rang out from the sky. \"Sister, I'm home!\"","She had thought she would have so many things to say. She would ask if her little sister was doing well, what the immortal sect was like, and whether Jiajia had forgotten their home in Big Tree Village. But all she did was lift her arms and wrap them tight around her little sister.","Qin Jia buried her face in her elder sister's shoulder, her voice muffled. \"Sister, I missed you so much.\"","Qin Zhen's eyes turned red, and she gently rested her hand on top of her little sister's head. \"I missed you too.\""]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: The First Appearance of Spiritual Plants","paragraphs":["More than half a year had passed since the sisters were reunited.","When they had last met, Qin Jia had excitedly told her family that she had successfully drawn qi into her body and officially embarked on the path of cultivation. She was now practicing the Ice Spirit Art personally imparted by her master, Perfected Person Binghua. In addition to cultivating every day, she also had to learn to read, identify spiritual medicines, and familiarize herself with the various rules of the cultivation world.","According to Qin Jia, her master, Perfected Person Binghua, was the strongest person in the Qingyun Sect beneath the Deity Transformation realm. Knowing that her younger sister was doing well in the Qingyun Sect, the heavy stone that had long hung over Qin Zhen’s heart finally sank halfway.","Although Linxian City had the character “immortal” in its name, it was still part of the mortal world. It was called Linxian only because the city housed a teleportation array connected to the cultivation world, through which cultivators occasionally came and went.","For mortals to enter the cultivation world through the teleportation array, it was by no means enough to simply pay some silver. The spiritual energy in the cultivation world was extremely abundant, while mortal meridians were far too fragile to withstand its impact. At best, their meridians would be damaged, leaving them bedridden for the rest of their lives. At worst, all their meridians would rupture and they would die on the spot.","This was not because the Qingyun Sect deliberately barred them. Their bodies simply could not withstand it.","Still, the matter was not entirely without a solution. If mortals consumed spiritual rice, spiritual vegetables, or low-grade spiritual plants with gentle medicinal properties over a long period of time, their meridians could be slowly nourished. It might take as little as three to five years, or as long as more than a decade. As long as they consumed enough spiritual food, their meridians would gradually adapt to spiritual energy.","The reason those princes, nobles, wealthy merchants, and powerful families in the city had moved their entire households to Linxian City was likely because they were clinging to that faint glimmer of hope.","The Qin family had already accepted this reality. They lived near Linxian City, and being able to see Qin Jia once a year was far better than being separated from her forever.","That was until Qin Jia brought back more than a dozen boxes of spiritual plant seeds.","There was no spiritual energy in Linxian City. Seeds left there would almost certainly never sprout. The Qin family did not tell Qin Jia this.","Yet the instant the seeds were buried in the soil, Qin Zhen felt an overwhelming hunger. The sensation did not belong to her. It came from the seeds underground.","Ever since she was very young, Qin Zhen had been able to sense the condition of plants. She knew which vegetables lacked water, which weeds had insects in their roots, and which trees, though seemingly lush with foliage, had already begun to rot inside.","When she was little, she had once cried in fear as she told her mother that the vegetables in the fields were speaking to her. Liu Zhen had assumed she had suffered a nightmare and gently soothed her, never taking the matter to heart. As Qin Zhen gradually grew older and realized that no one else possessed such an ability, she never mentioned it to anyone again.","But the sensations transmitted by the spiritual plant seeds were much clearer than those of ordinary plants. Waves of hunger and weakness seemed to appear directly inside her mind.","Without thinking, Qin Zhen pressed her palm against the soil. A faint warmth welled up from deep within her body, traveled down her arm into her palm, and finally seeped into the earth. The seeds underground, which had been restless and uneasy, gradually quieted down.","On the morning of the third day, the first tender shoot broke through the soil. After that, more and more seeds began to sprout. Seeds that should have rotted in ordinary soil came back to life one after another under her care. This even included several seeds that had already shriveled and blackened, having nearly lost all vitality.","Half a year passed, and the once-barren land behind the house had become lush and green.","Qin Zhen crouched at the edge of the field and placed her hand on a stalk of spiritual rice. The rice leaves trembled gently, and a feeling of fullness and joy came through them.","Qin Zhen touched several of the surrounding stalks in turn.","They were ripe.","“Zhenzhen, are you looking at the things you planted again?”","Liu Zhen returned from the mountain spring carrying a bucket of water.","Qin Zhen withdrew her hand, stood up, and brushed the dirt from her clothes. “Mother, this spiritual rice is ready. It should be ready to harvest tomorrow.”","“So soon?”","Liu Zhen walked to the edge of the field and looked at the heavy ears of rice in surprise. “Can it really be eaten?”","Wang Sumei had been drying wild vegetables in the courtyard. Upon hearing them, she hurried over as well. She stared at the spiritual rice in the field for a long while, her wrinkled face breaking into a broad smile.","“That’s wonderful. This old woman has lived for so many years, yet I’ve never eaten anything that immortals eat.”","Liu Zhen laughed. “Mother, Jiajia already said that this is merely the most ordinary spiritual rice, not some elixir of immortality.”","“The most ordinary spiritual rice is still spiritual rice.” Wang Sumei beamed. “Even the wealthy lords and madams in the city may not be able to get their hands on it.”","At those words, Qin Zhen’s gaze shifted slightly.","She knew that spiritual food was expensive. But exactly how expensive it was, no one in the Qin family knew.","The plot of land was not large. Qin Ye had originally estimated that, with the entire family working together, they could finish harvesting it in no more than one morning.","He walked into the field, grabbed a handful of rice stalks, and brought the sickle down.","Clang!","A crisp sound, like metal striking metal, rang out.","Qin Ye’s wrist went numb, and the sickle instantly bounced back. If he had not reacted quickly, the blade would have nearly slashed his arm.","“What happened?”","Qin Wen hurried over.","Everyone lowered their heads to look. A clear gap had been knocked into the sickle’s edge. By contrast, the rice stalks that had been struck only bore a faint white mark. Their outer skin had not even truly been broken.","Unwilling to believe it, Qin Ye moved to another spot and swung down with all his strength. The result was the same. After several strikes, the sickle’s edge had been completely bent, yet not a single stalk of spiritual rice had fallen.","“It looks just like rice, so how is it harder than wood?” Qin Ye frowned.","Qin Huai pondered for a moment. “These are ultimately things from the cultivation world. I’m afraid ordinary iron tools can’t be used to harvest them.”","Qin Wen suddenly remembered something. “Didn’t Jiajia bring back a sword last time?”","The sword had been an ordinary longsword given by the Qingyun Sect for its disciples to practice sword techniques. Qin Wen quickly retrieved it from the house.","Most items from the cultivation world required spiritual energy to activate. Qin Ye gripped the sword hilt with both hands and brought it down forcefully toward the spiritual rice. The instant the blade touched the stalk, an invisible resistance came up through the sword. The entire weapon suddenly grew heavy. No matter how much strength Qin Ye exerted, the blade could not move down even half an inch.","Qin Wen took the longsword and tried as well, but the result was the same.","“Looks ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍like this won’t work either.” Qin Ye reluctantly lowered the sword. “Since even this spiritual rice is an immortal object, perhaps only a cultivator can harvest it.”","“Then we’ll wait until Jiajia comes back next time.” Wang Sumei looked at the heavy ears of rice in the field. Though disappointed, she had no other choice.","“Father, let me try.”","Qin Ye froze. “This sword is heavy. You won’t be able to lift it.”","“I’m not going to swing the sword.” Qin Zhen looked toward the spiritual rice in the field. “I just want to see whether I can make it help me cut the rice.”","Although Qin Ye did not understand what she meant, he still handed her the sword.","The moment the longsword fell into her hands, Qin Zhen’s arm sank sharply. As expected, she could not truly wield the weapon.","She crouched down, gripping the sword hilt with one hand while gently pressing her other hand against the base of a nearby stalk of spiritual rice. A faint warmth welled up from deep within her body and flowed through her palm into the rice’s roots and stalk.","The spiritual rice in the field began to sway gently.","Just then, a faint breath of energy traveled along the leaves of the spirit rice and returned to Qin Zhen’s body. It was not the vitality she sent into the spirit plants every day, but a wisp of spiritual energy that the plants had naturally accumulated within themselves after ripening.","That wisp of spiritual energy flowed along her arm into her other hand before finally sinking into the hilt of the sword.","Hum...","The longsword suddenly let out an almost imperceptible, clear ring. A faint blue-green light appeared along the previously dim patterns on its blade.","Qin Zhen abruptly opened her eyes.","The longsword, which had felt as heavy as a mountain moments ago, had become slightly lighter. It was not completely weightless, but she could now slowly lift it.","She had not even truly swung the sword. The few stalks of spirit rice nearest to her simply bent to one side on their own. Their cuts were smooth and even, without damaging a single grain.","The field fell silent at once.","Qin Ye and Qin Wen stared at the faintly glowing longsword in Qin Zhen’s hand, momentarily forgetting to speak.","Wang Sumei stood stunned for a long while before cautiously asking, “Zhenzhen, do you have a spiritual root too?”","Qin Zhen’s face paled slightly. She shook her head. “Master Chen tested me. I don’t have a spiritual root.”","Qin Ye looked at the longsword in her hand. “Then how were you able to make it move?”","Qin Zhen lowered her gaze to the hilt. “I don’t know. Perhaps... they were helping me.”","She looked toward the gently swaying spirit rice before her.","The moment she finished speaking, the blue-green light on the blade rapidly dimmed. The heavy force pressed down on her arm once more. Qin Zhen nearly lost her grip on the sword and hurriedly planted its tip against the ground.","She had only cut down a few stalks of spirit rice, yet a thin layer of sweat had already appeared on her forehead.","Qin Huai noticed that something was wrong with her complexion and immediately said, “Don’t push yourself.”","Qin Zhen shook her head. “They’ve already ripened. If we don’t harvest them soon, the rice heads will weigh down and break the stalks.”","She placed her hand against the leaves of the spirit rice once more. A gentle, familiar emotion again reached her from the plants in the field.","After resting for a while, Qin Zhen borrowed another wisp of spiritual energy and slowly awakened the longsword.","Her body swayed. Liu Zhen hurried forward to support her. “Zhenzhen, are you feeling unwell?”","“No.” Leaning against her mother’s arms, Qin Zhen took a gentle breath. “I’m just a little tired.”","She looked toward the field, which had now been completely harvested.","The plot of land had seemed small, but in the end, it had yielded more than twenty pounds of spirit rice. Even uncooked, it gave off an exceedingly faint, pleasant fragrance.","Wang Sumei scooped up a handful of spirit rice, beaming with delight. “We’ll cook some tonight and have a taste.”","Qin Zhen reached out to stop her. “Grandmother, don’t cook too much. There’s a very strong force within this spirit rice. We can’t eat much at once.”","She could not explain how she knew. The moment her fingers touched the rice, she could sense the gentle yet abundant energy contained within it.","To cultivators, this spiritual energy might be insignificant. But the Qin family had never come into contact with spiritual energy before. If they ate too much at once, they might not be able to withstand it.","Wang Sumei had already grown accustomed to following Qin Zhen’s instructions regarding the fields. Hearing this, she took out only a small handful.","That evening, Liu Zhen mixed the small amount of spirit rice with ordinary millet and cooked it into a thin porridge. Once it was ready, each person received only half a small bowl.","The spirit rice was soft and sticky, with a hint of delicate sweetness. After drinking half a bowl of spirit porridge, the soreness in Qin Huai’s legs eased considerably. Wang Sumei had worked hard all her life and usually slept restlessly at night, but that day she fell into a deep sleep not long after lying down and did not wake once throughout the night.","The next morning, every member of the Qin family clearly felt somewhat lighter and more energetic upon waking. The change was not particularly dramatic, but it was enough to prove that the rumors circulating in the city were true.","Spiritual food really could nourish the bodies of ordinary people.","Inside the wooden house, the Qin family sat gathered together.","Qin Ye stared at the cloth bag for a long time, hesitation showing on his face. “I’m thinking of going into the city to ask around and find out where this spirit rice actually came from.”","The moment Qin Zhen heard this, she immediately shook her head in opposition. “Father, no. We can’t expose ourselves. It’s far too dangerous.”","“Zhenzhen is right.” Qin Huai’s expression darkened as he looked at Qin Ye in disapproval.","“Understood, Father. Then I’ll continue hunting in the mountains.”"]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: Broken Promise","paragraphs":["Qingyun Sect, Coldjade Peak.","The chill deep within the ice lake grew heavier with each passing day. Qin Jia sat cross-legged upon the Coldjade Platform at the center of the lake, a faint white mist coiling around her. Ice-attribute spiritual energy continuously gathered into her body, and she could vaguely sense that she had touched an invisible barrier.","Perfected Person Binghua stood by the lake and watched for a long while before finally speaking.","“Your cultivation can no longer be suppressed.”","Qin Jia opened her eyes.","“Master, am I about to break through?”","“Yes.”","Perfected Person Binghua raised a hand, and a streak of spiritual light entered the center of Qin Jia’s brow.","“Your cultivation has advanced too quickly, and the spiritual power within your body has yet to fully solidify. During this retreat, you must not only break through to the next realm but also reorganize the spiritual energy flowing through your meridians.”","“It may take as little as two or three years, or as long as several decades.”","Qin Jia had been beaming with joy, but the smile on her face froze at those last words.","“Several decades?”","She counted on her fingers, then suddenly sprang to her feet atop the Coldjade Platform.","“No!”","“I still have to go home this year.”","Perfected Person Binghua shot her a glance.","“An opportunity to break through may vanish in an instant. If you return to the mortal world and then come back, you may miss this chance entirely.”","Qin Jia lowered her head and looked at the Heartbond Pendant at her chest. The pale-green crescent-shaped jade pendant glimmered faintly. After hesitating for a long while, she finally asked, “Then can I send a message to my family first?”","“You may.”","Perfected Person Binghua did not stop her.","“Find ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍a disciple who will be traveling to Neighboring Immortal City soon and have him deliver a letter for you.”","With permission granted, Qin Jia immediately hurried down Coldjade Peak. She did not know many people within the sect. Senior Sister Chen Su was away on a sect mission and would not be returning anytime soon. Most of the other disciples had never been to Neighboring Immortal City. After thinking it over, Qin Jia decided that Senior Brother Xu An was the most suitable person.","Xu An was an inner disciple who often escorted supplies for the sect in exchange for contribution points, traveling back and forth between its various branches. Like Qin Jia, he had once been brought back from the mortal world, so they had quite a bit in common. However, as cultivators, both of them were busy with their own affairs, and they were not particularly close. A few days earlier, he had mentioned that he would soon be passing through Neighboring Immortal City.","When Qin Jia found him, he was outside the Teleportation Hall, counting jade slips.","“Senior Brother Xu!”","Xu An turned around. When he saw her, a smile quickly spread across his face.","“What brings you here, Junior Sister?”","Qin Jia took a communication jade slip from her storage pouch and solemnly held it out to him.","“Are you going to Neighboring Immortal City?”","“I leave tomorrow.”","“Then could you help me deliver this to my family?”","Worried that he might not be able to find them, Qin Jia carefully explained, “They live at the foot of the mountains west of Neighboring Immortal City. There are three wooden houses there, with a large patch of plants growing behind them.”","“My father’s name is Qin Ye, and my sister’s name is Qin Zhen. You should be able to find them if you ask around nearby.”","Xu An accepted the jade slip.","“What did you write inside?”","“I told them that I’m going into seclusion to break through, and that I may not be able to return for the next few years. I won’t be able to leave freely while I’m in seclusion, and I don’t know when I’ll emerge. You must tell them that I haven’t run into any danger and that they shouldn’t worry.”","After thinking for a moment, she took another jade box from her storage pouch.","“This is for my sister as well. There are some spirit seeds inside that I found recently.”","Xu An accepted both the jade slip and the jade box.","“It’s nothing, Junior Sister. Don’t worry. Once I reach Neighboring Immortal City, I’ll deliver them personally.”","Only then did Qin Jia relax.","“Thank you, Senior Brother.”","With that, she took out another jade box and handed it to Xu An.","“This is a small token of my appreciation. I’m sorry to trouble you, Senior Brother.”","Xu An took the box and smiled. “There’s really no need for this.”","The next day, Qin Jia entered the secluded cultivation chamber deep within Coldjade Peak. After the stone door closed, Perfected Person Binghua personally activated the formation outside the chamber. Until Qin Jia successfully completed her breakthrough, no one would be able to disturb her.","That same day, Xu An departed Qingyun Sect with the sect’s convoy. However, the communication jade slip was ultimately never delivered to the Qin family, and the jade box containing the spirit seeds never found its way into Qin Zhen’s hands.","Outside Neighboring Immortal City, summer in the mountains seemed especially long. When the time of year for Qin Jia’s annual homecoming arrived, the Qin family had tidied the house early. Liu Zhen made all the snacks her daughter used to enjoy, while Qin Ye and Qin Wen did not go into the mountains for several days in a row. They simply waited at the foot of the mountain, glancing up at the sky from time to time.","The Heartbond Pendant at Qin Zhen’s chest continued to glow. They waited from dawn until sunset, but the pendant never changed.","On the first day, the Qin family was not overly worried. Perhaps something had delayed her for a day or two—the affairs of an immortal sect were surely numerous. But after three days, Qin Jia still had not appeared. After ten days, the sky remained empty of the familiar streak of sword light.","Liu Zhen could no longer sit still. Qin Ye and Qin Wen took Qin Zhen into Neighboring Immortal City, where they asked around outside the teleportation array. The people guarding the array had never heard of Qin Jia, and they certainly were not going to contact Qingyun Sect on behalf of a few mortals.","Qin Ye tried asking people to approach the cultivators entering and leaving the teleportation array, but those cultivators were always in a hurry.","Some ignored them completely. Others complained that they were in the way. A few merely left them with a single remark:","“It’s perfectly normal for a disciple of an immortal sect to spend decades in seclusion or traveling.”","The Qin family could only return home in disappointment.","A month passed, and Qin Jia still had not come back. Although the light on the Heartbond Pendant had weakened, it had never gone out, and no cracks had appeared across the surface of the jade. This meant that Qin Jia was still alive.","Qin Huai could only console everyone.","“Perhaps Jiajia is in seclusion. It’s not unusual for cultivators to spend several months cultivating.”","The Qin family accepted this explanation and continued to wait.","They waited for an entire year.","When the appointed day arrived the following year, the Qin family once again went into the city and stood outside the teleportation array for seven full days. Qin Jia still did not appear.","In the third year, they paid a merchant who often did business with cultivators to inquire about Qingyun Sect.","The merchant took their silver, but returned with only one vague response:","“Everything is as usual at Qingyun Sect.”","As for where Qin Jia was, whether she was in seclusion, or when she might emerge, outsiders had no way of knowing.","It was not that the Qin family had never tried to find her.","Over the years, whenever they heard that a cultivator had entered Neighboring Immortal City, they would find a way to approach and ask about her. They had even asked others to deliver letters to Qingyun Sect, but they never received a response.","They had done nearly everything they could. The only proof that Qin Jia was still alive was the thin thread of azure light on Qin Zhen’s chest, which had never once gone out.","At the same time, the Qin family’s life was quietly changing as well.","After the first harvest of spirit rice, Qin Zhen kept most of it as seed. As she grew increasingly familiar with that mysterious power, the fields behind the wooden house gradually expanded.","At first, there had only been a few plots of land. Later, there was one mu, then two. Eventually, even the slopes below the mountain were cultivated into spirit fields. Though there was no spiritual energy in the area, the spirit rice and spirit vegetables continued to grow under Qin Zhen’s care.","Every day, the Qin family ate some of them.","One year, two years, three years...","The power within the spirit food gradually seeped into their flesh and meridians. Qin Huai’s once-graying hair slowly returned to its original black, while the hidden injuries Qin Ye and Qin Wen had sustained in their youth healed one after another. Liu Zhen and Wang Sumei’s health also became far better than before.","Although they had no spiritual roots and still could not absorb spiritual energy on their own, their bodies were no longer those of ordinary mortals. The changes in Qin Zhen were especially apparent. As the years passed, her sensitivity to spirit plants grew increasingly acute.","All these years, she had never stopped studying her ability. Little by little, she came to realize that she might truly be capable of entering that place mortals could never reach.","In the fifth year, Qin Jia still had not returned. On the night her expected return date passed, the Qin family gathered around the table, yet no one spoke for a long while. Qin Zhen’s Heartlink Pendant lay on the table. The jade pendant still glowed, but that faint light could only prove that Qin Jia was still alive.","“I’m going to the cultivation world to find her.”","Qin Ye finally broke the silence.","“I’m Jiajia’s father. I can’t keep waiting like this.”","“Father, you can’t go.”","Qin Zhen immediately shook her head.","“We don’t know what the cultivation world is like. Father, you’re too straightforward. If you run into someone with ill intentions, it would be easy for them to trick you into revealing things about our family.”","Qin Ye frowned.","“That still doesn’t mean I can let a young woman like you take such a risk.”","“I’m not going deep into the cultivation world right away.”","Qin Zhen looked toward the depths of the forest.","“I’ll only try to see whether I can cross the barrier.”","The Qin family had hunted in the nearby mountains for years and had long since discovered an invisible barrier deep within the forest. The rocks and trees beyond it were clearly visible, yet whenever an ordinary person approached, they would be stopped by an unseen force. They had always suspected that this was the boundary between the mortal realm and the cultivation world.","In the past, none of the Qin family had dared to approach it for real. But things were different now. Five years of nourishment from spirit food had gradually allowed their meridians to adapt to spiritual energy. Qin Zhen could even activate the low-grade sword Qin Jia had left behind. She might not be able to cultivate, but that did not necessarily mean she could not enter the cultivation world.","Qin Huai remained silent for a long time before finally asking, “What will you do if you’re able to cross over?”","“I won’t go far. First, I’ll investigate the area around the barrier and find somewhere inhabited. Then I’ll think of a way to ask about the Qingyun Sect. If I can’t get in, I’ll return immediately. If I can, then at least it will prove that we still have a way to find Jiajia.”","Silence once again fell over the room. They had already waited five years. If they continued to stay here, all they could do was guard the faint glimmer on the pendant—they could accomplish nothing else.","At last, Qin Huai slowly closed his eyes and let out a heavy sigh.","“Let Zhenzhen go and try, but she may only move around near the barrier. If she notices anything wrong, she must return immediately.”","On the day of her departure, the sky was still pale with dawn. Qin Zhen changed into a coarse cloth outfit that was convenient for traveling, strapped the long sword her sister had left behind to her back, and hid a short knife at her waist. Her backpack contained ten pounds of ordinary rice, several spirit vegetables, and a small amount of dried spirit-rice seeds.","The ordinary food would help conceal her identity. As for the spirit plants, they were the only thing she could rely on in the unfamiliar cultivation world.","Before she left, Liu Zhen straightened her collar.","“Zhenzhen, whether you find Jiajia or not, don’t push yourself.”","Qin Ye tried several times to speak, but in the end, he merely placed a heavy hand on his daughter’s shoulder.","Qin Zhen nodded. “I know.”","She closed her fingers around the Heartlink Pendant at her chest, which still gave off a faint glow, then turned and walked into the forest."]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: Vegetation Leads the Way","paragraphs":["The moment Qin Zhen stepped through the barrier, an invisible force pressed head-on against her. The air all around seemed to thicken abruptly, and icy cold breath surged into her body through her nose and mouth, making her chest feel tight and sending a fine, throbbing ache through her meridians.","She staggered back half a step and instinctively grabbed the trunk of a nearby tree. So this is the Cultivation Realm? Qin Zhen closed her eyes, waiting for a long while, but the searing pain she had braced for never came. The strange breath flooding into her made her uncomfortable, but it did not actually harm her meridians. For five full years, she had eaten nothing but spiritual rice and spiritual vegetables every day, and sure enough, her body was already strong enough to withstand the spiritual energy of the Cultivation Realm.","Yet once she had adjusted to the sensation, she quickly noticed another problem. There was no path in sight at all. Towering ancient trees blocked out the sky, and thick vines coiled around one another, nearly sealing off the way ahead entirely. The fallen leaves on the ground had piled up for no one knew how many years, and when she stepped down, they almost reached her ankles.","Qin Zhen looked back, and the barrier was still there behind her. Through that invisible shield, the mountains and forests of the mortal realm were clearly visible, so close she felt she could reach out and touch them. She carved a mark on a nearby tree, then tightened the strap of her bag and set off heading south.","Qin Jia had once mentioned that the Qingyun Sect lay to the south of the barrier. As long as she kept walking south, she would eventually find a place where people lived. The first few days of Qin Zhen's journey were extremely tough. The machete she had brought along could only cut through ordinary weeds. When it came to slightly thicker vines, the blade could not even leave more than a faint white mark on them.","As ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍for the long sword Qin Jia had left her, it was so heavy it felt like a solid lump of iron. Without spiritual energy to power it, it was no different from any ordinary iron weapon in the mortal world. Fortunately, this mountain forest had more plants than anywhere else, and unlike the vegetation of the mortal realm, every single plant here looked extraordinarily vibrant.","When Qin Zhen pressed her palm against a tree trunk, she could sense the faint emotions coming from the wood. Some were calm, some were wary, and some would even stretch out their branches and leaves of their own accord when she drew near. She could even sense through the tangled roots beneath the ground where there was water nearby, and where edible fruits grew.","By the seventh day, the dry rations she had brought were almost gone. Following the faint guidance from an old tree, Qin Zhen found a patch of low bushes bearing green berries beside a mountain stream.","She did not pluck them rashly. She rested her fingers on the leaves for a moment, sensing no danger, only then did she pick one, take a careful bite. The flesh was sweet and sour, and after she swallowed it, a faint wisp of warmth slowly spread through her abdomen.","After that, she survived on wild fruits, roots and clear spring water as she traveled. When she encountered vines she could not cut through, she would place one hand on the nearby plants, draw out the thinnest strand of spiritual energy from them, and use that to power her long sword for a short time.","The sword would only glow for a brief moment each time, but that moment was more than enough for her to slice through the vines blocking her way. However, each time she used it, she would be exhausted for a long while, so she would never draw the sword unless it was absolutely necessary.","The mountain forest was not devoid of wild beasts. On the twelfth night, Qin Zhen was jolted awake all of a sudden. Her chest felt tight, and all the plants around her sent her a strong sense of unease. Deep in the darkness, a pair of scarlet eyes could faintly be seen staring at her. Qin Zhen did not move. She slowly tightened her grip on her long sword and pressed her palm against the root of the tree behind her.","A warm current flowed from her palm into the soil. The next moment, the drooping vines nearby silently lifted up, piling layer upon layer in front of her, giving off a rich scent of plants and trees.","The wild beast in the darkness lingered for a long time, but in the end it did not come close. It was not until that dangerous aura had completely faded away that Qin Zhen realized her back was soaked through with cold sweat. The only things she could rely on were these silent plants all around her. Qin Zhen drifted off to sleep again, and when she opened her eyes, she found she was almost completely buried in grass.","\"What's going on?\"","Last night before she fell asleep, she had clearly cleared the area around her, but after just one night, the grass that had only reached her ankles had now grown as tall as her waist. The slender leaves brushed lightly against her arm, conveying a feeling of affection and joy.","Qin Zhen reached out and touched the grass blades, and the grass immediately scrambled to press toward her palm.","They seemed to love the aura coming from her body. Qin Zhen looked down at her own hand, puzzled.","Since she had entered the Cultivation Realm, her connection with the plants had grown clearer and clearer. Every time she fell asleep, that wisp of warmth inside her body seemed to seep out on its own. The plants of the mortal realm would only become a little more lively after absorbing that warmth, but the vegetation of the Cultivation Realm already contained spiritual energy. Once they received her power, their growth rate would become astonishingly fast.","\"Could this really be because of me?\"","Qin Zhen was full of questions, but she had no time to delve into them. She gently brushed the grass aside.","\"I have to keep going.\"","The grass blades clung to her clothes' hem reluctantly, and Qin Zhen patted the leaves to soothe them. The grass then slowly loosened, lying flat to both sides to make a narrow path for her.","Qin Zhen froze for a moment. This was the first time plants had responded to her thoughts so clearly. She walked along the path the grass had made for her.","That day, all the plants in the mountain forest seemed to know she was looking for an exit. Vines pulled their branches back of their own accord, and low shrubs parted to both sides. Whenever she walked in the wrong direction, the leaves nearby would send a wave of anxious emotion.","Guided by the plants, her speed increased a great deal. Three days later, the towering ancient trees that had blocked out the sky gradually thinned out, and sunlight spilled down through the gaps in the canopy. Qin Zhen quickened her steps, pushed aside the last patch of shrubs, and the view before her opened up completely."]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: South Pacify City","paragraphs":["In the distance, an enormous city stood nestled among the mountains. Its walls rose dozens of zhang high, their entire surface a lustrous white, as though the city had been carved from a single block of jade. Beneath the sunlight, they gleamed with a cool, crystalline sheen.","High in the air, great immortal cranes spread their wings, each bearing robed cultivators upon its back. Nearing the city gates, they folded their wings and descended slowly. From even higher above, streaks of sword light occasionally flashed past, while other cultivators rode spirit beasts of every shape and kind along the mountain roads.","Qin Zhen stood on the hillside for a long while without moving. Only now did she truly realize that she had entered a world utterly different from the mortal realm. So this was the sort of place her younger sister had lived in all these years.","She ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍took a deep breath and hurried toward the city.","Above the gates were three imposing characters, their strokes sharp and forceful. Qin Zhen could not read them, but from the conversations of those waiting to enter, she learned the city’s name—Southward Comfort City.","Southward Comfort City depended on the Azure Cloud Sect. Cultivators came and went here, but many ordinary people unable to cultivate also lived within the city, so mortals were not barred from entering.","Qin Zhen followed behind the crowd and passed through the gates without trouble. Her attention was immediately drawn to the sights within the city. All manner of shops lined the broad streets in orderly rows. Some sold medicinal pills, others weapons, while before many storefronts were displayed spirit plants and materials from spirit beasts that Qin Zhen had never seen before.","Qin Zhen could not read the signs, but fortunately, many shops had simple symbols carved beside their plaques. A cauldron signified a pill-refining shop, a longsword a weapon-forging workshop, and a leaf a store that sold spirit plants. Qin Jia had told her all this the last time she returned home.","The streets bustled with people. Some cultivators had palm-sized spirit birds perched upon their shoulders, while others cradled long-eared spirit beasts in their arms. Qin Zhen was curious, but she did not dare stare at anyone for too long, only stealing an occasional glance.","What she needed most now were spirit stones. Gold and silver from the mortal world could buy nothing in the cultivation world. After observing the shops along the street for some time, Qin Zhen finally stopped before an elegantly decorated establishment.","A gauzy curtain, thin as cicada wings, hung across the entrance. Through it, she could clearly see tables and chairs inside, as well as patrons eating their meals.","It seemed to be a restaurant. Qin Zhen lifted the delicate curtain and stepped inside. The moment she entered, a rich, inviting fragrance washed over her.","It had been a long time since she had eaten a proper meal. At the scent of food, her stomach gave a soft rumble. A woman dressed in a crimson-red gown came forward to greet her. She first glanced at the mud-stained hem of Qin Zhen’s clothes, then noticed the longsword on her back, yet her face showed no disdain.","“Little girl, are you here to eat?”","Qin Zhen shook her head.","“Big sister, I don’t have any spirit stones.”","The woman paused slightly. Qin Zhen continued, “I’ve just come out of the mountains and am looking for work in exchange for food and a place to stay.”","“I can chop firewood, carry water, and clean the courtyard.”","The woman looked Qin Zhen over from head to toe. Though the little girl’s clothes were worn and tattered, she was neat and clean, and she spoke clearly. She did not seem like one of the ordinary beggar children in the city. Still, Fragrant Elegance Pavilion already had enough servants and had no need for more hands.","The woman was about to refuse when a quarrel suddenly erupted from the rear courtyard.","“This batch of Green Jade vegetables was perfectly fine yesterday. How did they all wilt overnight?”","“Manager, I truly wasn’t slacking off!”","“I watered them exactly as the spirit-plant master instructed. The spirit-gathering formation is working properly too, but they just won’t recover.”","“The City Lord’s Manor is hosting a banquet tomorrow. If we can’t gather enough spirit vegetables, how is Fragrant Elegance Pavilion supposed to answer for it?”","Qin Zhen had not paid much attention at first. But when the door to the rear courtyard was pushed open, an overwhelming sensation of discomfort and suffocation suddenly flooded her mind.","Her steps halted, and she looked over instinctively.","Dozens of wooden crates stood neatly arranged in the courtyard. Each crate held several palm-sized green spirit vegetables.","Their leaves still appeared emerald-green, but their edges had begun to curl slightly. From their roots, a heavy, pained emotion continuously reached Qin Zhen.","It was not a lack of water, nor was it a shortage of spiritual energy.","They could not breathe.","Qin Zhen stared at the crates for a long while. The woman in crimson robes followed her gaze.","“Do you know Green Jade vegetables?”","Qin Zhen shook her head. “No.”","“Then what are you looking at?”","Qin Zhen hesitated before answering, “The soil beneath them is packed too tightly. Their roots are blocked. They can’t breathe.”","The courtyard immediately fell silent. Then a gray-clad attendant could not help but laugh.","“Plants can breathe?”","“Where did this little girl come from? Don’t spout nonsense here.”","Yet the woman did not immediately drive her away. This batch of Green Jade vegetables was worth no small sum. The city’s spirit-plant master had already examined them and said that the spiritual energy might be out of balance, advising them to increase the supply of spirit stones. But the spirit stones in the spirit-gathering formation had already been replaced twice, and the Green Jade vegetables had only grown more wilted.","She looked at Qin Zhen. “Do you have a solution?”","Qin Zhen walked over to one of the crates and crouched beside it. She gently inserted her fingers into the soil. Though the surface was loose and soft, the earth beneath had hardened into compacted clumps.","More strangely, there was a layer of extremely fine white rootlets mixed within it.","Those rootlets did not belong to the Green Jade vegetables. They were entwined around the vegetables’ roots, quietly siphoning away the spiritual energy in the soil.","Qin Zhen closed her eyes. A greedy, restless emotion traveled up through her fingertips.","“There’s something else in the soil,” she said. “It has tangled itself around the Green Jade vegetables’ roots.”","The gray-clad attendant frowned. “We inspect them every day. How could there be anything in the soil?”","Qin Zhen did not argue. Following the place where that emotion was strongest, she brushed aside the soil and pulled a strand of white rootlet as thin as a hair from around the Green Jade vegetable’s roots.","Once it left the soil, it began to writhe like a living creature.","The crimson-robed woman’s expression changed at once.","“Spirit-Draining Vine!”","The seeds of the spirit-siphoning vine were extremely tiny and often mixed in with spiritual soil. When they first took root, they were almost impossible to notice. But once they entwined themselves around the roots of other spirit plants, they would rapidly drain away their spiritual energy. If Qin Zhen had not found them, this batch of jade-green vegetables would likely have withered completely within two or three days.","“Turn over the spiritual soil in every wooden crate!”","The woman immediately ordered,","“Pick out every last root of the spirit-siphoning vines. Not a single one can be left behind!”","The shop hands hurriedly got to work. However, the spirit-siphoning vines’ roots were tangled too tightly with those of the jade-green vegetables. Any carelessness could tear away the vegetables’ roots as well. Qin Zhen, meanwhile, could clearly sense where the vines were located.","“Here—there’s another one on the left. Don’t use too much force underneath; you’ll damage the main root.”","As she gave instructions, she held her palm near the leaves of the jade-green vegetables. A faint warmth flowed from within her body, and the curled leaves gradually unfurled. The pain they conveyed to her also eased considerably.","About an hour later, all the spirit-siphoning vines had finally been cleared away. Su Qingqing personally inspected the plants. The jade-green vegetables that had been treated first were already standing tall again, their leaves restored to their former sheen.","The way she looked at Qin Zhen immediately changed.","“Are you a spirit plant cultivator?”","Qin Zhen shook her head. “I’ve never learned any spells for cultivating spirit plants. I’ve just always been rather good at growing things.”","Su Qingqing clearly did not entirely believe her. Even spirit plant cultivators had failed to notice the spirit-siphoning vines, yet Qin Zhen had located them so precisely. How could she merely be “rather good at growing things”?","But Qin Zhen was unwilling to say more, and Su Qingqing did not press the matter. Everyone had their own secrets.","“My name is Su Qingqing. I’m the proprietor of Fragrant Elegance Pavilion.”","She took five low-grade spirit stones from her storage pouch and handed them to Qin Zhen.","“The batch of jade-green vegetables you saved is worth far more than this. But as a mortal, carrying too many spirit stones would only make you an easy target for trouble.”","“These five spirit stones are your reward for today.”","Then she pointed to a small room in the back courtyard.","“Fragrant Elegance Pavilion has been needing someone to tend to its spirit vegetables.”","“If you are willing, you may stay here for the time being and help inspect the spirit vegetables delivered each day. I’ll provide food and lodging, and pay you another ten low-grade spirit stones every month.”","Qin Zhen did not agree immediately.","“I still need to find my younger sister. She is a disciple of the Azure Cloud Sect.”","Su Qingqing raised her brows slightly.","“The Azure Cloud Sect?”","Qin Zhen nodded. “Her name is Qin Jia. She hasn’t returned home in five years. We have received no news from her, so I entered the cultivation world to look for her.”","Su Qingqing considered this for a moment.","“The Azure Cloud Sect has countless disciples. It won’t be easy to make inquiries based on a name alone. However, South Fufeng City falls under the Azure Cloud Sect’s jurisdiction, and Fragrant Elegance Pavilion receives many Azure Cloud Sect disciples every day. If you stay here and work, it may be more convenient than searching the streets by yourself.”","Qin Zhen’s heart stirred. She had only just arrived and could not read the writing of the cultivation world. Nor did she know where the Azure Cloud Sect’s mountain gate was located. Even if she did encounter one of its disciples, they might not be willing to pay attention to an unfamiliar mortal. Staying at Fragrant Elegance Pavilion was indeed the safest and most practical option for now.","“Alright,” Qin Zhen said earnestly.","“I’ll stay, but only until I find my younger sister.”","Su Qingqing smiled.","“Of course.”","She had an attendant prepare Qin Zhen a bowl of hot food, then instructed someone to lead her to a small room in the rear courtyard to rest. Sitting at the table and gazing at the steaming meal before her, Qin Zhen finally felt the tension that had gripped her for over a month ease somewhat.","At the very least, she had entered the world of cultivation—and found a place where she could get close to disciples of the Azure Cloud Sect."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: News","paragraphs":["“Zhenzhen has been gone for so long without sending any word. It seems she must have made it through safely.”","In the fields, Qin Huai swung his hoe, hacking up a weed that had just poked its head above the soil. Even as he worked, he could not help muttering about his granddaughter, who had gone so far away.","“I only hope she’s safe in there.”","Madam Wang sat beside the field ridge, weaving the vines they had just gathered. At those words, her hands paused slightly, and she too looked toward the forested mountains to the south.","“Yes. Ye and Wen go to the area near the barrier every day to take a look. They’re hoping for any sign of movement.”","Ever since Qin Zhen had passed through the barrier, her family had been unable to learn anything about her. They only knew that Qin Zhen had successfully entered the cultivation world, but not where she was now, whether she had found Qin Jia, or whether she had encountered any danger.","Qin Huai said nothing more. He merely swung his hoe with noticeably greater force than before.","At the same time, deep within Cold Jade Peak of the Azure Cloud Sect.","Cold air filled the sealed cave abode. Qin Jia sat cross-legged atop a platform of cold jade, a thin layer of frost covering her brows, eyes, and hair. Her eyes were tightly closed as the surrounding ice-element spiritual energy continuously surged into her body.","The half-moon-shaped jade pendant hanging against her chest suddenly flickered faintly.","A weak green light flashed and vanished in an instant. Qin Jia’s lashes trembled slightly.","“Elder Sister...”","A vague murmur faded into the icy air, and soon the cave abode fell silent once more.","Nanfeng City, the rear courtyard of Fragrant Elegance Residence.","“Little Zhen, I heard you’ve found out something about your younger sister?”","Su Qingqing leaned against the doorway, smiling as she looked at Qin Zhen, who was crouched beside the spirit field. Qin Zhen was checking each of the emerald-jade vegetables in the courtyard. She lightly brushed her fingertips over the green leaves, and only after confirming that none of the plants’ roots had any problems did she rise to her feet.","“Yes, Sister Su. Yesterday, one of the guests who came to Fragrant Elegance Residence for a meal happened to be an outer disciple of Cold Jade Peak.”","At the mention of this, Qin Zhen’s expression finally relaxed somewhat.","“She said that Jiajia is in seclusion on Cold Jade Peak, attempting a breakthrough. She’s not in any danger.”","Although that outer disciple did not know Qin Jia personally, Cold Jade Peak was home only to Perfected Person Binghua’s lineage. Qin Jia was Perfected Person Binghua’s direct disciple, and she had not appeared in the sect for several years. She was indeed most likely in seclusion.","At least, she had not encountered any danger.","“That’s wonderful news.”","Su Qingqing offered her congratulations with a smile before asking, “Now that you know your younger sister is safe, are you still planning to remain in Nanfeng City and wait for her to emerge from seclusion? When cultivators enter seclusion to attempt a breakthrough, it may take as little as several months or as long as several years.”","Qin Zhen shook her head.","“I’m not going to wait any longer. Since Jiajia was safe before entering seclusion, she’ll naturally return home once she comes out. I’ve been gone for so long, and my family must be terribly worried about me. I’ll go back first and tell them that my younger sister is safe.”","Hearing this, Su Qingqing immediately looked disappointed.","“You’re leaving so soon? I was hoping to keep you at Fragrant Elegance Residence forever.”","Over the past two months, Qin Zhen had not learned a single spirit-plant cultivation technique, yet she could easily identify problems with the spirit vegetables. Which plant needed water, which had insects in its roots, and which patch of spirit soil contained too much spiritual energy—she could determine all of it with near-perfect accuracy simply by touching it.","Fragrant Elegance Residence had employed spirit-plant cultivators before, but when it came to caring for spirit plants, not one of them could compare with Qin Zhen. Su Qingqing was reluctant to see her leave, but she had no intention of stopping her.","Leaving aside the fact that Qin Zhen had a younger sister who was a direct disciple of the Azure Cloud Sect, just this ability to care for spirit plants alone meant that her future achievements might be extraordinary.","“Little Zhen, when you become successful in the future, don’t forget about your sister here.”","Qin Zhen replied earnestly, “Don’t worry, Sister Su. The next time I come to Nanfeng City, I’ll definitely visit you. Thank you for taking care of me these past two months.”","If Su Qingqing had not taken her in, Qin Zhen might not even have had a place to stay when she first entered the cultivation world.","“All right, there’s no need to be so formal between us.”","Su Qingqing waved her hand.","“Go pack your things first. Near the east gate of Nanfeng City, there’s a teleportation formation leading to Neighboring Immortal City. Taking the teleportation formation will be much faster than crossing the mountains and forests again.”","Qin Zhen’s eyes immediately lit up.","“It can take me directly back to Neighboring Immortal City?”","“Of course.”","Su Qingqing could not help laughing.","“Otherwise, do you think everyone entering or leaving the cultivation world has to spend more than a month traveling through the mountains and forests like you did?”","Qin Zhen was delighted. She immediately turned and headed toward the small room where she lived.","“You little girl, why are you in such a hurry?”","Su Qingqing called out from behind her. Qin Zhen halted and turned back in confusion, only to see Su Qingqing take out a small cloth pouch and casually toss it over.","Qin Zhen hurriedly caught it. The pouch was surprisingly heavy. When she opened it, she found fifty lower-grade spirit stones neatly arranged inside.","“Sister Su, this is...”","“The teleportation formation costs fifty lower-grade spirit stones per use.”","Leaning against the doorframe, Su Qingqing spoke in a casual tone.","“Take them. They’re exactly enough to get you back to Neighboring Immortal City.”","Qin Zhen quickly held the pouch out again.","“No, Sister Su. This is too much.”","“I’ve been eating and staying at Fragrant Elegance Residence for the past two months without doing anything to repay you. Why don’t I stay for a few more months and return home after I’ve earned enough?”","“If you stay for several more months, your family will probably be frantic with worry.”","Su Qingqing did not take the pouch.","“These fifty spirit stones aren’t a gift. Consider them an investment I’m making in advance.”","She spoke half-jokingly. “If you really become some great spirit-plant master in the future, you mustn’t forget that you owe me this favor.”","Qin Zhen held the pouch in both hands and remained silent for a long while. She did not want to incur such a significant debt of gratitude for no reason.","But when she thought of her grandparents, parents, and uncle waiting at home for news of her, she found herself unable to refuse.","“Thank you, Sister Su.”","Qin Zhen carefully put away the spirit stones.","“I’ll remember what you’ve done for me today.”","“If I ever have the chance, I’ll repay you.”","“All right, that’s enough.”","Su Qingqing waved dismissively.","“Hurry up and pack. The teleportation formation can only be activated a limited number of times each day. If you miss the last trip today, you’ll have to wait until tomorrow.”","With that, she turned and walked into Fragrant Elegance Residence. Qin Zhen stood where she was, watching her retreating figure, and silently engraved this debt of gratitude in her heart.","Before long, she had packed her belongings. Compared to when she had first arrived in Nanfeng City, there was not much more in her bundle. The ordinary food her family had prepared for her before she left had already been eaten, leaving only a small bag of spirit-rice seeds and a few personal items.","Aside from those, she had only the small amount of spirit stones she had saved over the past two months.","Qin Zhen slung the bundle over her back, tied the long sword her younger sister had left behind across her back, and hurried toward the eastern part of the city. By the time she arrived at the teleportation formations, the sky had already begun to darken.","Several teleportation formations of various sizes were spread across the spacious plaza, with lines of people waiting before each one. Qin Zhen stood to the side and observed for a while. By following the symbols beside the formations and listening to the conversations of passing travelers, she finally located the line for Neighboring Immortal City.","She hurried over. The line was not particularly long, and it was soon her turn. The cultivator in charge of guarding the teleportation array sat behind a wooden desk. Without even looking up, he simply held out a hand.","“Fifty low-grade spirit stones.”","Qin Zhen handed over the spirit stones Su Qingqing had given her. The cultivator swept them with his divine sense, confirmed that the amount was correct, and raised a hand to point ahead.","“Go in. This is the last trip today. If you’re any later, you’ll have to wait until tomorrow.”","At that, Qin Zhen hurried into the teleportation array.","The array was circular, its floor carved with intricate silver patterns. Several dozen people were already standing inside. Qin Zhen could only carefully make her way to the outermost edge, doing her best not to bump into anyone.","Before long, the cultivator guarding the array embedded a spirit stone into the array’s core.","The patterns on the ground lit up one after another. Blinding white light shot into the sky, instantly enveloping everyone within.","In the next moment, every figure in the teleportation array vanished. Qin Zhen’s vision went white, followed immediately by a violent wave of dizziness. It felt as though countless forces were squeezing her from all directions at once. Her chest tightened, and her internal organs seemed to be churning together. Her legs went weak, and she nearly lost her balance.","Qin Zhen bit her lip hard, struggling to remain conscious.","She didn’t dare close her eyes. She knew the teleportation would take only a moment, yet time seemed to stretch endlessly. She had no idea how long passed before that suffocating pressure finally began to fade.","The solid ground returned beneath her feet. Qin Zhen steadied herself against a nearby stone pillar and cautiously opened her eyes.","The people around her looked just as miserable. Some had only just managed to regain their footing when they began complaining.","“The teleportation array in Nanfu City is getting worse and worse.”","“No kidding.”","Another person rubbed his chest, his face pale.","“I ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍wonder how long it’s been since they last repaired it. These past few years, every time I travel to the Mortal Realm, I have to suffer through this.”","“Do you really think the people in charge of the city care whether we live or die?”","“As long as the array can still operate and collect spirit stones, they can’t be bothered to spend money repairing it.”","“Next time, I’m not traveling from Nanfu City.”","“I’d rather take the long way around and use the teleportation array in Yuxian City.”","Someone beside them shook his head when he heard that.","“The teleportation array in Yuxian City is stable enough, but each trip costs two hundred low-grade spirit stones.”","“Nanfu City is the closest to the Mortal Realm and charges only fifty. Other than here and Yuxian City, there isn’t a third teleportation array to the Mortal Realm anywhere nearby.”","“Even if it costs more, it’s still better than suffering.”","“That’s easy for you to say. You have the spirit stones.”","The group continued grumbling as they walked out of the teleportation array.","Qin Zhen stood among the crowd, her face still somewhat pale, but her heart was already overflowing with joy.","Linxian City.","She was finally home.","Qin Zhen tightened her grip on the Heartbound Pendant at her chest. Ignoring her physical discomfort, she hurried out of the teleportation array. She couldn’t wait to return home.","To tell everyone...","Jiajia hadn’t met with any misfortune. She was merely in secluded cultivation."]}]);
